CHAPTER.VERS:
But draw near here, you

          {+}
         sons of the psychic, the seed of the adulterer and the prostitute.

Against whom do you

          {+}
         sport yourselves? Against whom do you

          {+}
         make a wide mouth, and put out the tongue? Are you

          {+}
         not children of transgression, a seed of falsehood,

you

          {+}
         who inflame yourselves among the oaks, under every green tree; who slay the children in the valleys, under the clefts of the rocks?

And he will say, Cast

          {+}
         up, cast

          {+}
         up, prepare the way, take up the stumbling-block out of the way of my people.
